Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Add=20scene=20save=20(Ctrl+S)=20=E2=80=94=20per?=
 =?UTF-8?q?sist=20entity=20edits=20back=20to=20scene.json?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SceneLoader was load-only: the inspector tracks each entity's
Authored transform and lets you edit position/rotation/scale, enabled
state, name, and light live, but none of it survived exit.

SceneLoader.Save() writes the scene's current entity state back to
the file it was loaded from. Each Entity keeps a reference to the
EntityDefinition it was built from (SceneLoader._sources), so Save()
only ever overwrites the fields the inspector can actually edit —
name, enabled, transform, light — and carries everything else
(model/material bindings, uv, components, triplanar overrides)
forward unchanged from what was originally authored.

Bound to Ctrl+S in InputSystem, ahead of the ImGuiWantsKeyboard gate
so it works regardless of UI focus, mirroring Escape/mode-toggle.

Scoped out for now (flagging, not silently dropped):
- Multi-file ("include") scenes: flattened into one in-memory entity
  list at load with no record of which file an entity came from, so
  Save() has no correct per-entity destination. SceneLoader.CanSave
  reports this; the current scene.json doesn't use include, so it's
  unaffected.
- Camera position/skybox exposure/black-level edits: not persisted
  yet (Save() carries these through from the originally loaded
  definition unchanged) — schema already supports both, so this is a
  natural, low-effort follow-up if wanted.
- Per-instance material property edits (Color/Roughness/Metallic/
  Translucency, editable in the inspector's Material section): the
  scene schema only supports material *bindings* (paths), not inline
  scalar overrides, so these aren't round-trippable without a schema
  extension — out of scope here.

Verified via a temporary in-engine test hook (mutate an entity, call
Save(), inspect the written JSON, then reverted) against a headless
run: name/position/enabled round-tripped correctly, light serialized
with the right fields, model/material bindings and camera/skybox
definitions passed through unchanged.
